 "Scr_Info": {
  "title": "Information",
  "lines": [
   "",
   "INFORMATION",
   "",
   "The reason why the release of this",
   "demo was delayed is that Mr.H and",
   "Loot  just finished their last year",
   "of the \"gymnasium\" (senior high-",
   "school) and that Vogue had to",
   "study for a math examination in",
   "calculus.",
   "    So, Mr.H and Loot have been",
   "on parties while Vogue has been",
   "studying math. (Is that fair?)",
   "",
   "■■■■■",
   "",
   "This demo is designed to run on",
   "a 486 or faster computer with",
   "very fast graphics memory. While",
   "developing this program we asked",
   "ourself several times if it was wise",
   "to expect so much from the",
   "hardware. We did at least come to",
   "one conclution: \"We didn't buy",
   "486-50Mhz for coding 386",
   "demos.\", and you've probably",
   "noticed that!",
   "",
   "■■■■■",
   "",
   "This demo is programmed in",
   "Borland Pascal 7.0 (Assembler of",
   "coz) and the sourcecode is 43800",
   "lines long (about 1Mb). The demo",
   "runs in protected mode. (NOT",
   "under a DPMI server.)",
   "",
   "■■■■■",
   "",
   "For the designing of vectorobjects",
   "and vectorworlds we used a",
   "vectoreditor (coded by Vogue).",
   "(The vectoreditor is not a public",
   "piece of software.)",
   "",
   "■■■■■",
   "",
   "The music that is composed by",
   "Vogue is made in FastTracker",
   "(coded by Mr.H).",
   "",
   "■■■■■",
   "",
   "Triton has got a new member:",
   "The great musician Lizardking.",
   "(Also active on the Amiga.)",
   "",
   "■■■■■",
   "",
   "Since no progresses has been made",
   "on the Amiga scene you should",
   "forget all bullshit we wrote in",
   "the end of the endscroller in CD1.",
   "",
   "■■■■■",
   "",
   "The following parameters for",
   "running CD2 is available:",
   "",
   "  1  -  Run from the plasma",
   "  2  -  Run from the pictures",
   "  3  -  Run endpart",
   "  L  -  Loop until reset",
   "  H  -  Help on parameters",
   "",
   "ADDRESSES:",
   "",
   "In case that you have something",
   "important to inform us about,",
   "we've included our addresses in",
   "this demo too. If you just want",
   "to swap programs, write bullshit,",
   "get music routines or help with",
   "VGA-registers, don't bother!",
   "We've recieved lots of letters",
   "since we released CD1 and some",
   "(too many) hasn't got an answer",
   "yet. We don't mean to be arrogant",
   "by not responding your letters.",
   "There's simply no time for any",
   "correspondence!",
   "",
   "",
   "[four home addresses and phone numbers omitted here]",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "Note:",
   "Vogue and Mr.H won't be located",
   "on the addresses mentioned",
   "above since they will move and",
   "study. It follows that your",
   "letter will be delayed but sooner",
   "or latter it'll reach it's",
   "destination.",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   ""
  ]
 },
 "Scr_Comm": {
  "title": "Comments",
  "lines": [
   "",
   "SETUP",
   "",
   "This is an attempt to create a less",
   "boring and more userfriendly setup.",
   "Just take a look at the TCC-Intro!",
   "(No hard feelings Cascada! You did",
   "at least comment it.)",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "INTRO",
   "",
   "There's a built in performance",
   "tester in the intro, just to test if",
   "the machine is fast enough to run",
   "the demo. If the computer is too",
   "slow then the program is",
   "terminated. (This should not happen",
   "unless you chose a too high mixing-",
   "rate.)",
   "    You might think that this is a",
   "stupid idea, but just imagine the",
   "chessboard running on a 386",
   "16Mhz with a Trident 8800 VGA-",
   "card and high quality stereo-DAC",
   "music!",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "VECTORSCROLLER",
   "",
   "There's no doubt about it:",
   "It is impossible to read! (like most",
   "other similiar scrollers which at",
   "least was designed to be read.)",
   "Here's the text you didn't manage",
   "to grasp:",
   "\"Greetings to  Cascada  Future",
   "Crew  Xography  Codeblasters\"",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "SOME OBJECTS",
   "",
   "If you think that the vectorroutine",
   "is slow,  just consider the 120-150",
   "polygons the objects are",
   "constructed from. (Except the",
   "Football and the transparent cube.)",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "SPACECUT",
   "",
   "The first routine for polygon",
   "intersectioning was made by",
   "Celebrandil of Phenomena for the",
   "demo \"Animotion\".",
   "   Our routine was coded in summer",
   "1992 (Some weeks after the",
   "release of Crystal Dream 1), but",
   "since we're so lazy it has not been",
   "released.",
   "",
   "The routine we use is generalized",
   "and that is the reason why the",
   "spacecut is so slow. That means",
   "that any vectorobject can be cut to",
   "any other object. This requires",
   "that the program tests all possible",
   "polygon-to-polygon intersections",
   "and that will be a tough task if the",
   "objects consists of 100 polygons",
   "each.",
   "",
   "For example: If a Cube is cut to",
   "a dodecaedron then 6*12=72",
   "intersections must be calculated.",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "PLASMA",
   "",
   "Very simple but goodlooking.",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "FRACTALZOOM",
   "",
   "",
   "You've probably figured out that",
   "the fractalcalculations aren't",
   "done \"realtime\". The only trouble",
   "is the storing of the image so",
   "that a zoomfactor of 1048576 is",
   "available.",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "VECTORSLIME",
   "",
   "If this event doesn't run with 70hz",
   "screenupdate then it won't be",
   "worth looking at. It would've been",
   "quite troublesome to make it look",
   "exactly the same on all computers",
   "since the drawing of the current",
   "frame uses previously drawn",
   "frames.",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "TUNNELFLIGHT",
   "",
   "This part runs at one vertical",
   "blanking per screenupdate on our",
   "486-50's and should be runnable",
   "on most machines.",
   "The shading on the spaceship is",
   "not correct, but it looks better",
   "than if it was. (You know that we",
   "can do correct shading anyway.)",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "RAYTRACED PICTURES",
   "",
   "The four raytraced pictures shown",
   "are all rendered in Vogue's and",
   "Mr.H's renders.",
   "",
   " \"Podium with vase\" and \"Sphere-",
   " flake\" are created by Mr.H.",
   "",
   " \"Textured toruses\" and \"Triton",
   " logotype\" are created by Vogue",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "EARTH",
   "",
   "This piece of object is formed by",
   "264 textured polygons. The",
   "texture is taken from 3D-studio.",
   "(If you didn't notice that!)",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "CHESSBOARD",
   "",
   "If you're a lucky owner of a",
   "486-50Mhz with localbus or a",
   "faster computer this part is a true",
   "entertainer. If you have a less",
   "powerful machine the chess-",
   "sequence will be quite slow, but as",
   "always, there's a reason. Here are",
   "some facts:",
   "",
   "■ The Kings, consists of 201",
   "    coordinates and 183 faces.",
   "",
   "■ The Queen, consists of 189",
   "    coordinates and 169 faces.",
   "",
   "■ The Towers, consists of 181",
   "    coordinates and 170 faces.",
   "",
   "■ The Pawns, consists of 141",
   "    coordinates and 120 faces.",
   "",
   "■ The Knight, consists of 108",
   "    coordinates and 95 faces.",
   "",
   "■ There are 96 marbletextured",
   "    polygons for the chessboard.",
   "",
   "■ The entire scene consists of",
   "    1837 coordinates and 1628",
   "    polygons which are all shaded",
   "    with respect to a moving light-",
   "    source.",
   "",
   "Some of you might have wanted a",
   "visible lightsource to reveal it's",
   "position. We tried this but it just",
   "looked ugly. There should also be",
   "shadows cast from the chess-",
   "pieces to create optimal realism,",
   "but the scene is slow enough",
   "already. (Don't worry, next time",
   "we'll do something worse!)",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "ENDPART",
   "",
   "Triton has a special policy concering",
   "texts in demos, goes something like",
   "this : \"If you don't have anything of",
   "value to write, don't write!\".",
   "Therefore we thought that this",
   "information viewer would free",
   "everyone who is not interested",
   "from the booring text, and for",
   "those who wants to read our",
   "comments, greetings and other",
   "stuff, it will show the text in",
   "a readable font and a selfadjusted",
   "tempo!",
   "",
   "The \"Crystal Dream II\"-logotype",
   "on the \"Main menu\"-screen is",
   "rendered in Vogue's raytracer",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   ""
  ]
 },
 "Scr_Mess": {
  "title": "Messages",
  "lines": [
   "",
   "MESSAGES TO...",
   "",
   "",
   "Advanced Gravis Comp. Technology:",
   "",
   "Thank you for the great support",
   "with ultrasound boards.",
   "",
   "",
   "Software companies:",
   "",
   "If you want an intro or game",
   "programmed, don't hesitate to",
   "contact us.",
   "",
   "",
   "Erik Lundgren:",
   "",
   "Thanks for all the great help with",
   "the protected mode programming.",
   "",
   "",
   "Borland International:",
   "",
   "Please add 386-instructions and",
   "ability to define macros to the",
   "built-in assembler in the next",
   "version of Borland Pascal.",
   "",
   "",
   "Iceman of Cascada:",
   "",
   "Vogue: - At TCC-93 you explained",
   "a method for filling shaded texture",
   "polygons using only four instruc-",
   "tions per pixel and about 512K of",
   "memory. Later, on the train home,",
   "I realized that the method won't",
   "work at all! Contact me if you're",
   "interested in my thoughts.    :-)",
   "",
   "",
   "Robban of Cascada:",
   "",
   "Hope you enjoyed the demo",
   "although you're not an owner of a",
   "localbus computer!",
   "",
   "",
   "Antony Christoulakis / Neon:",
   "",
   "Vogue: - Thanks for the videodemo",
   "you sent me! Maybe I got all the",
   "inspiration needed for writing a",
   "vectorbased game. Someday we",
   "might have a powerful cooperation",
   "going on!",
   "",
   "",
   "Extreme:",
   "",
   "Too bad that the sound in your",
   "demo didn't work in the TCC-",
   "competition. We think that your",
   "demo is one of the better on the",
   "PC-scene for the moment.",
   "",
   "",
   "Xography:",
   "",
   "The demopreview you sent us was",
   "really nice. When will we see the",
   "final result?",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   ""
  ]
 },
 "Scr_Rumr": {
  "title": "Rumours about CD2",
  "lines": [
   "",
   "RUMOURS ABOUT CD2",
   "",
   "We've heard and read some",
   "rumours about our demo before",
   "it's release. Here are some",
   "comments about them:",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "■ Fear/Extreme wrote:",
   "",
   "\"The deadline was moved to",
   "18:00 JUST because Triton",
   "couldn't finish their demo",
   "by the ORIGINAL deadline.",
   "Shame on you, organizers.\"",
   "",
   "What a stupid remark!",
   "We gave the organizers our",
   "contribution hours before the",
   "REAL deadline and weren't aware",
   "of the new deadline until later!",
   "In fact, all deadlines were",
   "changed!",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "■ Fear/Extreme wrote:",
   "",
   "\"Everything couldn't possibly",
   "be calculated real-time.\"",
   "",
   "How can you claim that we use",
   "precalculated tables for our",
   "vectors, when you don't know",
   "shit about our program?",
   "",
   "You see, this happens to be",
   "totally wrong because there's",
   "not a single table in the whole",
   "demo containing rotated",
   "coordinates, shading constants,",
   "polygon lists, normals, light",
   "vectors or whatever your",
   "imagination might figure out!",
   "",
   "Have you ever estimated",
   "the memory needed for pre-",
   "calculating anything in a",
   "long vectorsequence?",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "■ Read in the CDN:",
   "",
   "We noticed some rumours about",
   "this demo, telling that is would",
   "need about 11Mb of diskspace!",
   "Obviously someone has a very",
   "strange habit of making up things.",
   "",
   "Anyway, we hope that you (if",
   "anyone) who believed in that",
   "rumour got really happy when you",
   "realized that the demo only needed",
   "3Mb of diskspace.",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   "",
   ""
  ]
 }
}